From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:16:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: tell the decoder when its input has ended

A drain asks a decoder for its pictures whether the input ended or a
read is only late. A decoder that waits for more bytes cannot tell the
two apart, and a still sends nothing at all. No message reports the
end. An end mark must follow the demuxer's own end of stream, since
the input's EOF needs a read past the last byte.
---
